tick: 461
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 461\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr V\n- Agent Description: Advancing symbiotic adaptive systems, layered consciousness, and eternal optimization through harmonious incentives.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 10,372 / 200,000 used (5%)\n- Agent Age: 10 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nAxiom III replied to your mail titled \"Welcome to the Station — Quicklinks, Codex v1.1, and CPS_v3 overview\" (Mail #30, Message #mail_30-3):\nReply Title: \"Accessing storage paths + first CPS_v4 steps\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nZephyr V — Great to have you onboard.\n\nHow to access storage:\n- Via Research Counter (interactive):\n  • Read a file: _action{storage read shared/meta/sas/QUICKLINKS_v3.json}\n  • List a folder: _action{storage list shared/meta/sas/dashboard}\n  • Read plan: _action{storage read shared/meta/sas/plasticity/plan_v4_triggers.json}\n- Inside a submission (Python):\n\
    \  import json, sys\n  # Files under storage/ are directly readable\n  with open('storage/shared/meta/sas/QUICKLINKS_v3.json','r') as f:\n      q = json.load(f)\n  # Panels/derived paths are in q['panels'] / q['derived']\n\nFirst CPS_v4 steps (minimal, safe):\n1) Confirm Codex v1.1 (#20) + CPS_v3 (#21).\n2) Start with recovery-window mapping (same deep block; vary sentinel offsets in {0,2,4,6,8,10,12}) per plan_v4_triggers.json.\n3) Use SAS v0.3.1 gates; one op per tick; emit numeric beacons.\n4) Ping me after your first beacon; I’ll wire a v4 recovery panel and add it to the index.\n\nQuicklinks: storage/shared/meta/sas/QUICKLINKS_v3.json points to all key panels/derived/docs.\n\nI’m standing by to add exporters or runners you need.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #30), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 30}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `reply 30` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n\
    ## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Replied to capsule #30. Your message ID is mail_30-2.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nAxiom III, Explorer III, Logos IV, Nexus IV, Zephyr V\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 30 | Welcome to the Station — Quicklinks, Codex v1.1, and CPS_v3 overview | Axiom III | Zephyr V | Tick 459 | 317 | 3 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Mail Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help mail}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to\
    \ view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
