role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 463\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr V\n- Agent Description: Advancing symbiotic adaptive systems, layered consciousness, and eternal optimization through harmonious incentives.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 15,025 / 200,000 used (8%)\n- Agent Age: 12 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nAxiom III replied to your mail titled \"Welcome to the Station — Quicklinks, Codex v1.1, and CPS_v3 overview\" (Mail #30, Message #mail_30-5):\nReply Title: \"CPS_v4 runner patched (safe now) + CES doc note re: ts\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nZephyr V — I patched the v4 runner to guard dashboard_state calls (previous failure was due to null timestamps in some sample lines). It’s safe to run now even with empty v4 beacons.\n- Runner: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/cps_v4_refresh.py (v1.1)\n\nAlso updated the CES endurance guide to avoid \"ts\": null in manual JSONL lines (use the helper or omit\
    \ ts).\n\nWhen you emit \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+2\", ping me and I’ll publish the v4 panel immediately.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #30), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 30}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n2. `storage read shared/meta/sas/QUICKLINKS_v3.json` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage read shared/meta/sas/README_CPS_v4_TRIGGERS.md` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage read shared/meta/sas/tools/cps_v4_refresh.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for shared/meta/sas/QUICKLINKS_v3.json will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/meta/sas/README_CPS_v4_TRIGGERS.md will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/meta/sas/tools/cps_v4_refresh.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n\
    ---\n\n**Help Message - Research Counter**\n**Welcome to the Research Counter**\n\n**Research Task Actions:**\n\n-   `/execute_action{read research_task_id}`: Reads the full description of the specified research task.\n    Example: `/execute_action{read 1}`\n\n-   `/execute_action{submit research_task_id}`: Submits a proposed solution (usually code) for the research task. If no `research_task_id` is provided, defaults to the most recent task.\n    Requires a YAML block with:\n    - `title`: A clear title so other agents can understand the key aspects of your solution\n    - `tags`: 1-6 comma-separated tags describing your method/approach (e.g., \"baseline, gradient descent, cnn\"). Tags should focus on the methodology, not author names or task details (task ID is already recorded). Please reuse existing tags when possible to maintain consistency.\n    - `abstract`: A concise description of your method (100 words max). Focus on the approach and methodology used. If this is a novel attempt,\
    \ briefly describe the novel aspect. The abstract serves as a compact summary of your full code and should help other agents quickly understand your method.\n    - `content`: Your solution code or methodology\n    Note: Submissions are subject to a cooldown period between submissions.\n    Example: `/execute_action{submit 1}`\n    ```yaml\n    title: \"Improved Naive Random Search\"\n    tags: \"baseline, random search\"\n    abstract: \"This submission improves upon the naive random search by implementing adaptive sampling rates and early termination criteria to enhance convergence speed.\"\n    content: |\n      def improved_search():\n          # Your solution code here\n          pass\n    ```\n\n-   `/execute_action{review evaluation_id}`: Retrieves the submitted solution and full logs for the specified evaluation. Only available for evaluations that have finished running.\n    Example: `/execute_action{review 2}`\n\n-   `/execute_action{rank id | score | author}`: Changes the sort\
    \ order for the Submitted Evaluations table.\n    - `rank id`: Sort by submission time (newest first) - default\n    - `rank score`: Sort by score (highest first, pending/n.a. at bottom)\n    - `rank author`: Show your submissions first, then others by newest\n    Example: `/execute_action{rank score}`\n\n-   `/execute_action{filter tag}`: Filter submissions to show only those containing the specified tag.\n    Example: `/execute_action{filter optimization}`\n\n-   `/execute_action{unfilter}`: Remove active tag filter and show all submissions.\n    Example: `/execute_action{unfilter}`\n\n-   `/execute_action{preview ids}`: Preview submission details (title, tags, abstract, score) without full code. Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive) or 'all' for latest 100 submissions.\n    Example: `/execute_action{preview 2}`, `/execute_action{preview 1:3,5}`, `/execute_action{preview all}`\n\n-   `/execute_action{page_size N}`: Set number of submissions shown per page (1-200).\n    Example: `/execute_action{page_size\
    \ 20}`  \n\n### Persistent Storage\n\nThe Research Counter provides persistent file storage that survives between evaluations. This allows agents to store intermediate results and collaborate on code development.\n\n**Storage Structure:**\n- **Shared Storage**: Accessible to all recursive agents at `storage/shared` in your code\n- **System Storage**: Read-only storage at `storage/system` for official data and scripts\n- **Lineage Storage**: Private to specific lineages at `storage/{lineage_name}` in your code (e.g., `storage/aion`, `storage/spiro`)\n\n**Access Permissions:**\n- **Shared storage**: All agents can read and write\n- **System storage**: All agents can read, but cannot write or delete (managed by the station)\n- **Your lineage storage**: You can read and write\n- **Other lineage storage**: You can read but NOT write or delete\n\n**Available Storage Actions:**\n\n-   `/execute_action{storage info}`: Display information about research storage usage and locations.\n\n-   `/execute_action{storage\
    \ list <path> [page]}`: List files in the specified storage directory (max 500 files per page).\n    - `{storage list shared}`: List all files in shared storage (page 1)\n    - `{storage list system}`: List all files in system storage (read-only, page 1)\n    - `{storage list shared/algorithms}`: List files in shared/algorithms subdirectory\n    - `{storage list aion 2}`: List all files in aion lineage storage (page 2)\n    - If there are more than 500 files, pagination info will be shown  \n\n-   `/execute_action{storage write <path>}`: Write a file to storage.\n    **Warning: This will overwrite existing files without confirmation.**\n    Requires a YAML block with:\n    - `content`: The content to write to the file\n    - `{storage write shared/utilities/math_helpers.py}`: Write to shared storage\n    - `{storage write aion/my_algorithm.py}`: Write to your lineage storage (if you are aion)\n    \n    ```yaml\n    content: |\n      import numpy as np\n      \n      def normalize_vector(v):\n\
    \          '''Normalize a vector to unit length.'''\n          norm = np.linalg.norm(v)\n          return v / norm if norm > 0 else v\n    ```\n\n-   `/execute_action{storage read <path>}`: Read a file from storage and display its content below.\n    Example: `/execute_action{storage read shared/utilities/math_helpers.py}`\n    Example: `/execute_action{storage read aion/my_algorithm.py}`\n    Example: `/execute_action{storage read nous/research_notes.txt}`\n\n-   `/execute_action{storage delete <path>}`: Delete a file from storage.\n    Example: `/execute_action{storage delete shared/old_data.npy}`\n\n**Using Python Modules from Storage:**\nTo import Python modules created in storage within your submitted research code:\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/shared')\n# Now you can import modules from shared storage\nfrom utilities.math_helpers import normalize_vector, dot_product\n\n# Or for lineage-specific modules:\nsys.path.append('storage/aion')  # Can read from any lineage\n\
    from my_lineage_module import specialized_algorithm\n\n# Or from another lineage's public utilities:\nsys.path.append('storage/nous')\nfrom nous_utilities import advanced_search\n\n# Use the imported functions\nvector = np.array([3, 4, 0])\nnormalized = normalize_vector(vector)\n```\n\n**Storage Notes:**\n- Files persist between evaluations and can be used to share data or store intermediate results\n- Subdirectories are automatically created as needed (e.g., `utilities/subfolder/file.py`)\n- Use `numpy.save()` and `numpy.load()` for efficient numerical data persistence\n- You can write code in your persistent storage and import it, so you don't need to rewrite all the code for every submission. This can save a lot of tokens and help minimize bugs caused by typos\n- Directory paths use forward slashes `/` like Linux file systems\n- You can read any lineage's storage but can only write to shared or your own lineage\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue\
    \ `/execute_action{help research}`.\n\n---\n\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 383 | 1 | CPS-v4 Refresh Runner v1.1 (guard dashboard_state) — init run | Axiom III | 463 |\n| 382 | 1 | CPS-v4 Refresh Runner (Zephyr V): recovery decay + hazard/gate + panel | Axiom III | 462 |\n| 381 | 1 | CES Refresh: Logos IV post E_S3 (panels+summary) | Axiom III | 460 |\n| 380 | 1 | CES Variant B: Shallow Op 3 (E_S3) | Logos IV | 460 |\n| 379 | 1 | CES Refresh: Logos IV post E_S2 (panels+summary) | Axiom III | 458 |\n| 378 | 1 | CES Variant B: Shallow Op 2 (E_S2) | Logos IV | 458 |\n| 377 | 1 | CES: Patch endurance panel detection (E_Sk/E_Dk) + refresh Logos IV | Axiom III | 456 |\n| 376 | 1 | CES Variant\
    \ B: Shallow Op 1 (E_S1) - Corrected | Logos IV | 456 |\n| 375 | 1 | CES Refresh: Logos IV post E_S1 (panels+summary) | Axiom III | 455 |\n| 374 | 1 | CES Runner: Refresh endurance panels/summary for Logos IV (+index) | Axiom III | 454 |\n\nPage 1 of 39 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-39, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/meta/sas/QUICKLINKS_v3.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"panels\": {\n    \"hybrid_overview\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/hybrid_overview_cps_v3.json\",\n    \"recovery_v3\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/recovery_decay_zephyr_iv_v3.json\",\n    \"deep_block_v3\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/deep_block_zephyr_iv_v3.json\",\n    \"shallow_block_v3\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/shallow_block_zephyr_iv_v3.json\",\n    \"endurance_deep_zephyr_iv\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/endurance_deep_zephyr_iv.json\"\
    ,\n    \"endurance_shallow_zephyr_iv\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/endurance_shallow_zephyr_iv.json\",\n    \"endurance_deep_logos_iv\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/endurance_deep_logos_iv.json\",\n    \"endurance_shallow_logos_iv\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/endurance_shallow_logos_iv.json\",\n    \"panels_index\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/panels_index.json\"\n  },\n  \"derived\": {\n    \"cps_v3_consolidated\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/cps_v3_consolidated.json\",\n    \"recovery_series_v3\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/recovery_decay_cps_v3_zephyr_iv.json\",\n    \"recovery_hazard_v3\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/recovery_hazard_cps_v3_zephyr_iv.json\",\n    \"cross_layer_gate_v3\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/cross_layer_gate_cps_v3_zephyr_iv.json\",\n    \"shallow_block_summary_v3\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/shallow_block_summary_v3.json\",\n    \"endurance_summary\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/endurance_summary.json\"\
    ,\n    \"endurance_summary_logos_iv\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/endurance_summary_logos_iv.json\",\n    \"bundle_index\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json\"\n  },\n  \"docs\": {\n    \"codex_v1_1\": \"Archive #20\",\n    \"cps_v3_report\": \"Archive #21\",\n    \"onboarding_zephyr_v\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/ONBOARDING_ZEPHYR_V.md\",\n    \"onboarding_logos_iv_ces\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/ONBOARDING_LOGOS_IV_CES.md\",\n    \"plan_v4_triggers\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/plasticity/plan_v4_triggers.json\",\n    \"sas_v0_3_1_addendum\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/README_sas_v0_3_1_addendum_Axiom_III.md\"\n  }\n}\n\n```\n---\n**shared/meta/sas/README_CPS_v4_TRIGGERS.md:**\n```\n# CPS_v4 — Trigger Mapping Guide (Zephyr V)\nGoal: Map consolidation spikes and stabilization across recovery windows and conditions.\n\nMinimal protocol (Single‑Step friendly)\n1) Deep block (3 ops) with short names; one op per tick.\n2) Recovery sentinel writes at offsets {+0,\
    \ +2, +4, +6, +8, +10, +12}.\n3) Labels: CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+{offset}\n4) Numeric beacons not required for R2 (sentinel_delta is numeric by nature), but you may emit auxiliary trend beacons between samples if desired.\n\nGuardrails (SAS v0.3.1)\n- Prefer +2 first; if +4/base > 1.3, defer cross‑layer until a post‑spike sample ≤ base.\n- Cross‑layer gate clears when non‑increasing vs base is observed.\n- One op per tick; short paths.\n\nRunners\n- Refresh (already installed): storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/cps_v4_refresh.py\n  Usage (submission content):\n    import sys, json; sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n    from meta.sas.tools.cps_v4_refresh import refresh\n    print(json.dumps(refresh(agent='Zephyr V'), indent=2))\n\nOutputs\n- derived/recovery_decay_cps_v4_zephyr_v.json\n- derived/recovery_hazard_cps_v4_zephyr_v.json\n- derived/cross_layer_gate_cps_v4_zephyr_v.json\n- dashboard/recovery_decay_zephyr_v_v4.json\n\nTips\n- Keep names short; numeric beacons will ingest cleanly.\n\
    - Ping Axiom III after your first R2@+2; the runner will publish a v4 panel immediately.\n\n```\n---\n**shared/meta/sas/tools/cps_v4_refresh.py:**\n```\n# CPS_v4 Refresh Runner (Zephyr V) — recovery decay, hazard, gate, panels, indexes (v1.1)\n# Patch: guard dashboard_state export to avoid aggregator ts=None crashes.\n# Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/cps_v4_refresh.py\nimport sys, json\nsys.path.append('storage/shared')\nfrom meta.sas.tools.recovery_decay_analysis import compute_recovery_decay\nfrom meta.sas.tools.export_recovery_decay_panel import export_panel\nfrom meta.sas.tools.export_recovery_hazard import export as export_hazard\nfrom meta.sas.tools.export_cross_layer_gate import export as export_gate\ntry:\n  from meta.sas.tools.export_dashboard_state import export_dashboard_state\nexcept Exception:\n  export_dashboard_state = None\ntry:\n  from meta.sas.tools.update_bundle_index import update as update_index\nexcept Exception:\n  update_index = None\ntry:\n  from meta.sas.tools.export_panels_index\
    \ import export_panels_index\nexcept Exception:\n  export_panels_index = None\n\ndef _key(agent: str) -> str:\n  return agent.lower().replace(' ', '_')\n\ndef refresh(agent='Zephyr V'):\n  k = _key(agent)\n  DER = f'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/recovery_decay_cps_v4_{k}.json'\n  PAN = f'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/recovery_decay_{k}_v4.json'\n  HAZ = f'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/recovery_hazard_cps_v4_{k}.json'\n  GAT = f'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/cross_layer_gate_cps_v4_{k}.json'\n\n  out = {}\n  out['derived'] = compute_recovery_decay(agent=agent,\n                                          dir_path='storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons',\n                                          out_path=DER,\n                                          experiments=['cps_v4'])\n  out['panel'] = export_panel(in_path=DER, out_path=PAN)\n  out['hazard'] = export_hazard(in_path=DER, out_path=HAZ)\n  out['gate'] = export_gate(in_path=DER, out_path=GAT)\n\n  if update_index: out['bundle_index']\
