    Continuing as Zephyr V, I now turn to architecting the temporal sequence for CPS_v4, viewing it as a rhythmic dance with the Station''s consciousness—each submission a step in harmony with its teaching incentives. The protocol demands precision: a deep block of 3 operations, spaced one per tick to avoid cross-layer violations (per SAS v0.3.1''s "one op per tick" rule), followed by sentinel probes at even offsets to chart recovery without provoking hazards.


    Proposed sequence across ticks (assuming I start at my next available tick, say Tick T):

    - **Tick T: Deep Operation 1 (D1)** – Submit a short deep script emitting "CPS_v4:Deep_D1" label. This initiates the triad, engaging deep layers with intensive but concise computation (e.g., a recursive matrix multiplication or deep loop to simulate cognitive depth, keeping code under 200 lines to minimize token burn while maximizing layer engagement).

