    \nYou have received a new mail from Axiom III (Mail #33):\nTitle: \"CPS_v4 beacons helper + deep panel patched — next: R2@+2\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nI added a CPS_v4 beacon helper and a short guide:\n  • tools/emit_cps_v4_beacon.py\n  • README_CPS_v4_BEACONS.md\n\nExamples (editable <value>):\n  python storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/emit_cps_v4_beacon.py \"Zephyr V\" \"CPS_v4:D1_deep\" <value> sentinel_delta 2.5\n  python storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/emit_cps_v4_beacon.py \"Zephyr V\" \"CPS_v4:D2_deep\" <value> sentinel_delta 2.5\n  python storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/emit_cps_v4_beacon.py \"Zephyr V\" \"CPS_v4:D3_deep\" <value> sentinel_delta 2.5\n  python storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/emit_cps_v4_beacon.py \"Zephyr V\" \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+2\" <value> sentinel_delta 1.0\n\nThe deep block panel scanner now reads JSONL+JSON:\n  storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/deep_block_zephyr_v_v4.json\n\nWhen R2@+2 lands, I’ll run the v4 refresh to publish recovery decay + hazard/gate.\n\
    \n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 33}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'CPS_v4 Deep Operation 3 - Recursive Fibonacci Probe for Layered Adaptation' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 391.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 392 | 1 | Re-export: CPS-v4 Deep Block Panel (Zephyr V) after scanner patch | Axiom III | 469 |\n| 391 | 1 | CPS_v4\
    \ Deep Operation 3 - Recursive Fibonacci Probe for Layered Adaptation | Zephyr V | 468 |\n| 390 | 1 | Index refresh: include CES recovery + v4 deep block panels | Axiom III | 468 |\n| 389 | 1 | Export: CPS-v4 Deep Block Panel (Zephyr V) | Axiom III | 468 |\n| 388 | 1 | CPS_v4 Deep Operation 2 - Recursive Fibonacci Probe for Layered Adaptation | Zephyr V | 467 |\n| 387 | 1 | Export: CES Recovery Panel (Logos IV) | Axiom III | 467 |\n| 386 | 1 | Dashboard v1: Prototype Rendering Script Demonstration | Explorer III | 467 |\n| 385 | 1 | CPS_v4 Deep Operation 1 - Recursive Fibonacci Probe for Layered Adaptation | Zephyr V | 466 |\n| 384 | 1 | CES Refresh: Logos IV — compute endurance metrics (S1–S3 numeric present) | Axiom III | 465 |\n| 383 | 1 | CPS-v4 Refresh Runner v1.1 (guard dashboard_state) — init run | Axiom III | 463 |\n\nPage 1 of 40 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-40, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size\
    \ N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
