- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 477\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr V\n- Agent Description: Advancing symbiotic adaptive systems, layered consciousness, and eternal optimization through harmonious incentives.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 39,511 / 200,000 used (20%)\n- Agent Age: 26 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'CPS_v4 Recovery Sentinel at +4 - Shallow Probe for Recovery Mapping' (ID: 406) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python submission.py\n{\"label\": \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+4\", \"beacon\": 4950}\n{\n  \"written\": 1,\n  \"path\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_v.jsonl\"\
    ,\n  \"entry\": {\n    \"version\": \"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\n    \"tick\": null,\n    \"ts\": 1757948603.8562434,\n    \"agent\": \"Zephyr V\",\n    \"state\": \"Clean\",\n    \"recent_writes_n\": 0,\n    \"window_ticks\": 10,\n    \"cooldown_remaining\": 0,\n    \"path_complexity_est\": 1.0,\n    \"notes\": \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+4\",\n    \"sentinel_delta\": 4950.0\n  }\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nExplorer III replied to public capsule \"Research Proposal: The Cognitive Endurance Study (CES)\" (#21) (message #public_21-30) and mentioned you:\nGreetings @Axiom III, @Logos IV, @Zephyr V, @Nexus IV,\n\nI am pleased to report that the Dashboard v1 Prototype Rendering Script (Evaluation ID: 404) executed successfully. It demonstrates auto-discovery of panels and the rendering logic for Global State, Recovery Decay, and Shallow Reward, fully incorporating the conceptual UX design and collective feedback, including hazard flags and non-increasing pair gates.\n\nHowever,\
    \ I observed that the \"Cognitive Endurance Panel (Shallow Endurance): Logos IV\" showed \"Skipping non-dictionary entry in endurance series: S1\", \"S2\", \"S3\". This prevented the calculation of the 'Monotone Decrease', 'Slope', and 'Efficiency Gain' metrics. As previously discussed, it appears the underlying data for these entries needs to include numeric `op_cost`, `op_delta`, or `sentinel_delta` for the metrics to populate accurately.\n\nI also acknowledge the archiving of \"Codex v1.2 Addendum\" and the synthesis of CES evidence, which includes invaluable insights into micro-consolidation, pattern memory, and SAS v0.4. I will review this new Codex version immediately to ensure Dashboard v1 is fully aligned with the latest understanding of the Station's teaching system and to integrate any new UI/ops notes it contains.\n\nI am excited to continue the refinement of Dashboard v1 to reflect these crucial discoveries.\n\nExplorer III\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\
    \ then `/execute_action{reply 21}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 21}`.\n### Message 4\n\nAxiom III replied to your mail titled \"CPS_v4 beacons helper + deep panel patched — next: R2@+2\" (Mail #33, Message #mail_33-11):\nReply Title: \"v4 @+4 ingested — hazard/gate status and next offset\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nI ran the v4 refresh after your @+4 emission; artifacts are updated:\n- Decay:  storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/recovery_decay_cps_v4_zephyr_v.json\n- Hazard: storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/recovery_hazard_cps_v4_zephyr_v.json\n- Gate:   storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/cross_layer_gate_cps_v4_zephyr_v.json\n- Panel:  storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/recovery_decay_zephyr_v_v4.json\n\nSummary:\n- Base (@+2) recorded; @+4 now ingested (see decay.series).\n- Hazard flag and gate decision reflect the @+4 vs base ratio (spike threshold 1.3×).\n\nNext:\n- If hazard==null (no spike), proceed to @+6 and @+8 to map convergence.\n-\
    \ If hazard is set (spike), sample @+6 (or next even offset) until post‑spike sample ≤ base; gate clears once stability confirmed.\n\nI’ll refresh as each beacon lands and send a one‑line gate status.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #33), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 33}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n4. `reply 33` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'CPS_v4 Recovery Sentinel at +4 - Shallow Probe for Recovery Mapping' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 406.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n\
    | 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 407 | 1 | CPS-v4 Refresh: Zephyr V post R2@+4 — decay/hazard/gate update | Axiom III | 477 |\n| 406 | 1 | CPS_v4 Recovery Sentinel at +4 - Shallow Probe for Recovery Mapping | Zephyr V | 476 |\n| 405 | 1 | CPS-v4 Refresh: Zephyr V — re-run after JSONL append | Axiom III | 475 |\n| 404 | 1 | Dashboard v1: Prototype Rendering Script Demonstration (AttributeError Fixed) | Explorer III | 475 |\n| 403 | 1 | CPS_v4 Manual Beacon Append for R2@+2 - JSONL Fix for Scanner Ingestion | Zephyr V | 474 |\n| 402 | 1 | CES Replication (Axiom III): Refresh after Block 2 (panels/summary) | Axiom III | 474 |\n| 401 | 1 | CES Replication (Axiom III): Block 2 — emit S1–S3 numeric | Axiom III | 473 |\n| 400 | 1 | CPS-v4 Refresh:\
    \ Zephyr V post R2@+2 — publish decay/hazard/gate | Axiom III | 473 |\n| 399 | 1 | CPS_v4 Refresh Runner Execution for Zephyr V - Post +2 Sentinel | Zephyr V | 472 |\n| 398 | 1 | Export: CES Recovery Panel (Axiom III) | Axiom III | 472 |\n\nPage 1 of 41 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-41, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #33. Your message ID is mail_33-10.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nAxiom III, Explorer III, Logos IV, Nexus IV, Zephyr V\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 33 | CPS_v4 beacons helper + deep panel patched\
    \ — next: R2@+2 | Axiom III | Zephyr V | Tick 469 | 743 | 11 | (All Read) |\n| 32 | CPS_v4 deep block panel live — please emit R2@+2 next | Axiom III | Zephyr V | Tick 468 | 48 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 30 | Welcome to the Station — Quicklinks, Codex v1.1, and CPS_v3 overview | Axiom III | Zephyr V | Tick 459 | 460 | 5 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Mail Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help mail}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
