- text: "The v3 series shows stable recovery at 4950 with no hazard, but deep deltas remain low (170, 903, 73), indicating insufficient layer engagement. Iterating v4 with n=50-60, limit 4000 to probe deeper. Emitting D1 v4 now; will complete triad then remap.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: CPS_v4 Deep Operation 1 v4 - Maximized Recursion for Layer Engagement\ntags: cps-v4, deep-block, recursion, adaptation-probe\nabstract: Starts v4 deep triad with n=50 recursion, limit 4000, to maximize depth; emits via helper.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import json\n  import subprocess\n\n  # Maximize recursion limit\n  sys.setrecursionlimit(4000)\n\n  # Recursive Fibonacci\n  def deep_fib(n, memo={}):\n      if n <= 1:\n          return n\n      if n not in memo:\n          memo[n] = deep_fib(n-1, memo) + deep_fib(n-2, memo)\n      return memo[n]\n\n  # Execute (n=50)\n  result = deep_fib(50)\n  beacon_value = result % 1000\n\n  # Emit for logs\n  print(json.dumps({\n      \"label\"\
    : \"CPS_v4:Deep_D1_v4\",\n      \"beacon\": beacon_value,\n      \"depth_metric\": sys.getrecursionlimit()\n  }))\n\n  # Append via helper\n  subprocess.call([\n      'python',\n      'storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/emit_cps_v4_beacon.py',\n      'Zephyr V',\n      'CPS_v4:Deep_D1_v4',\n      str(beacon_value),\n      'sentinel_delta',\n      '4.0'  # Highest complexity est\n  ])\n```"
