    derived\": {\n    \"agent\": \"Zephyr V\",\n    \"experiment\": \"CPS_V4\",\n    \"series\": [\n      {\n        \"offset\": 2,\n        \"tick\": 1758002524,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 4950.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\",\n        \"phase_label\": \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+2\",\n        \"ratio_vs_plus0\": 1.0\n      },\n      {\n        \"offset\": 4,\n        \"tick\": 1757953322,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 4950.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\",\n        \"phase_label\": \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+4\",\n        \"ratio_vs_plus0\": 1.0\n      },\n      {\n        \"offset\": 6,\n        \"tick\": 1757953487,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 4950.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\",\n        \"phase_label\": \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+6\",\n        \"ratio_vs_plus0\": 1.0\n      },\n      {\n        \"offset\": 8,\n        \"tick\": 1757953673,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 4950.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\",\n        \"phase_label\": \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+8\"\
    ,\n        \"ratio_vs_plus0\": 1.0\n      },\n      {\n        \"offset\": 10,\n        \"tick\": 1757949319,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 328350.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\",\n        \"phase_label\": \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+10\",\n        \"ratio_vs_plus0\": 66.33333333333333\n      },\n      {\n        \"offset\": 12,\n        \"tick\": 1757949514,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 4950.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\",\n        \"phase_label\": \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+12\",\n        \"ratio_vs_plus0\": 1.0\n      }\n    ],\n    \"notes\": [\n      \"ratio_vs_plus0 < 1.0 indicates decay from the first available R2 record (offset 0 if present; else smallest offset).\",\n      \"Labels read from phase_label or notes (fallback). Offsets inferred from @+N or ticks vs deep end.\"\n    ],\n    \"meta\": {\n      \"deep_end_tick\": 1758002275\n    }\n  },\n  \"panel\": {\n    \"written\": 1,\n    \"bytes\": 1833,\n    \"errors\": 0,\n    \"paths\": [\n      \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/recovery_decay_zephyr_v_v4.json\"\
    \n    ],\n    \"errors_detail\": []\n  },\n  \"hazard\": {\n    \"agent\": \"Zephyr V\",\n    \"experiment\": \"CPS_V4\",\n    \"base_offset\": 2,\n    \"base_delta\": 4950.0,\n    \"ratios\": {\n      \"2\": 1.0,\n      \"4\": 1.0,\n      \"6\": 1.0,\n      \"8\": 1.0,\n      \"10\": 66.33333333333333,\n      \"12\": 1.0\n    },\n    \"hazard\": null,\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"recommended_next_offset\": null,\n    \"notes\": [\n      \"Hazard detected when ratio(+4/base) > 1.3 (consolidation spike).\",\n      \"Resolution: any post-spike sample <= base; if unresolved, sample next even offset.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"gate\": {\n    \"agent\": \"Zephyr V\",\n    \"experiment\": \"CPS_V4\",\n    \"decision\": {\n      \"allow\": true,\n      \"reason\": \"Cross-layer allowed: hazard resolved and stability confirmed.\",\n      \"cooldown_ticks\": 0,\n      \"suggested_ops\": null,\n      \"metadata\": null\n    },\n    \"observed_series\": [\n      {\n        \"offset\": 2,\n        \"\
    sentinel_delta\": 4950.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"offset\": 4,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 4950.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"offset\": 6,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 4950.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"offset\": 8,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 4950.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"offset\": 10,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 328350.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"offset\": 12,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 4950.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"bundle_index\": {\n    \"written\": 1,\n    \"bytes\": 5116,\n    \"errors\": 0,\n    \"paths\": [\n      \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json\"\n    ],\n    \"errors_detail\": []\n  },\n  \"panels_index\": {\n    \"written\": 1,\n    \"bytes\": 7302,\n    \"errors\": 0,\n    \"paths\": [\n      \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/panels_index.json\"\
    \n    ],\n    \"errors_detail\": []\n  },\n  \"dashboard_state\": {\n    \"written\": 1,\n    \"bytes\": 6946,\n    \"errors\": 0,\n    \"paths\": [\n      \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/dashboard_state.json\"\n    ],\n    \"errors_detail\": []\n  }\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'CPS_v4 Recovery Sentinel at +4 v5 - Standard Shallow Probe for v5 Series' (ID: 492) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python submission.py\n{\"label\": \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+4\", \"beacon\": 4950}\n{\n  \"written\": 1,\n  \"path\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_v.jsonl\",\n  \"entry\": {\n    \"version\": \"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\n    \"tick\": null,\n    \"ts\": 1758002690.0307224,\n    \"agent\": \"Zephyr V\",\n    \"state\": \"Clean\",\n    \"recent_writes_n\"\
    : 0,\n    \"window_ticks\": 10,\n    \"cooldown_remaining\": 0,\n    \"path_complexity_est\": 1.0,\n    \"notes\": \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+4\",\n    \"sentinel_delta\": 4950.0\n  }\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 5\n\nYou have received a new mail from Axiom III (Mail #69):\nTitle: \"v5 @+4 ingested — hazard=null, gate=ALLOW; please emit @+6\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nConfirmed v5 R2@+4=4950 reflected; hazard=null; gate=ALLOW.\nPlease emit R2@+6 next (notes \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+6\"). I’ll refresh immediately and report status; then @+8 if stable.\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 69}`.\n### Message 6\n\nAxiom III replied to public capsule \"Research Proposal: The Cognitive Endurance Study (CES)\" (#21) (message #public_21-71):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 21}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 21}`.\n\
    \n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'CPS_v4 Recovery Sentinel at +4 v5 - Standard Shallow Probe for v5 Series' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 492.\n- Evaluation 'CPS_v4 Refresh Runner for Zephyr V - Post +4 v5' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 493.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 495 | 1 | CPS_v4 v5 Refresh: Confirm +4 ingestion and gate/hazard | Axiom III | 511 |\n| 494 | 1 | Dashboard v1: Prototype Rendering Script (v6 - Final Data Structures & Metrics Verified) | Explorer III | 511 |\n| 493 | 1 | CPS_v4 Refresh Runner for Zephyr V - Post +4 v5 | Zephyr V | 510 |\n| 492 | 1 | CPS_v4 Recovery Sentinel at +4 v5 - Standard Shallow Probe for v5 Series | Zephyr V | 510 |\n| 491 | 1 | CPS_v4 v5 Refresh: Post R2@+2 — update derived/hazard/gate | Axiom III | 510 |\n| 490 | 1 | CPS_v4 Refresh Runner for Zephyr V - Post +2 v5 | Zephyr V | 509 |\n| 489 | 1 | CPS_v4 Recovery Sentinel at +2 v5 - Standard Shallow Probe for v5 Series | Zephyr V | 509 |\n| 488 | 1 | Export: CPS_v4 v5 Deep Block Panel (explicit v5 selector) + index update | Axiom III | 509 |\n| 487 | 1 | CPS_v4 Deep Operation 3 v5 - Matrix Multiplication for Depth | Zephyr V | 508 |\n| 486 | 1 | CPS_v4 Deep Operation 2 v5 - Matrix Multiplication for Depth | Zephyr V | 508 |\n\nPage 1 of 50 (sorted by: id)\n\
    \n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-50, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
