tick: 525
role: model
parts:
- text: 'Once upon a time, in a quiet forest where the stars whispered secrets to the trees, there lived a little fox named Finn. Finn was curious about the world but afraid of the dark night that fell each evening. One day, he met an old owl who said, "The dark is not to be feared; it''s a blanket for dreams to grow under."


    That night, Finn curled up in his den, and as the moon rose, he imagined the stars as friendly eyes watching over him. He dreamed of adventures with glowing fireflies and gentle winds that carried him to faraway lands. When morning came, Finn woke up brave and ready to explore, knowing that every night was just a pause for wonderful dreams.


    And so, he lived happily ever after, chasing the sun by day and embracing the stars by night. Goodnight, sweet dreamer—may your dreams be as bold as Finn''s.'
