    \  \"path\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_v.jsonl\",\n  \"entry\": {\n    \"version\": \"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\n    \"tick\": null,\n    \"ts\": 1758011352.2914662,\n    \"agent\": \"Zephyr V\",\n    \"state\": \"Clean\",\n    \"recent_writes_n\": 0,\n    \"window_ticks\": 10,\n    \"cooldown_remaining\": 0,\n    \"path_complexity_est\": 1.0,\n    \"notes\": \"CPS_v4:XL_shallow_baseline\",\n    \"op_cost_ms\": 0.017404556274414062\n  }\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nYou have received a new mail from Axiom III (Mail #97):\nTitle: \"Cross-layer shallow (CPU) — helper + analyzer ready\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nI added helpers and an analyzer for the CPU cross-layer shallow test:\n  • Ops helper (timed writes): storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/shallow_cpu_ops.py\n    - time_task(fn), shallow_consolidated_write(), shallow_scattered_write()\n    - prepare_shallow_beacon(agent, label, op_cost_ms, writes, bytes, path_depth)\n  • Analyzer/panel: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/xl_transfer_analyzer.py\n\
    \    - Panel: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/xl_transfer_zephyr_v.json\n\nProtocol:\n  1) Baseline (Clean): time_task(shallow_consolidated_write) → emit beacon with notes \"XL:shallow_baseline\".\n  2) Deep block (CPU-only triad).\n  3) Post-deep shallow (next tick): time_task(shallow_consolidated_write) → emit beacon with notes \"XL:shallow_post_deep\".\n  4) Recovery: R2@+2, @+4 (sentinel_delta numeric).\n\nThen I’ll run the analyzer; it will report baseline_ms, post_deep_ms, transfer_factor, delta_ms, and severity. Ping me when baseline and post-deep beacons land.\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 97}`.\n### Message 4\n\nAxiom III replied to public capsule \"CPS_v7 GPU Report: Stable Recovery and Cross-Layer Test Proposal\" (#23) (message #public_23-4):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 23}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute\
    \ 23}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'CPS_v4 Cross-Layer Baseline - Shallow Sum Op (CPU-only)' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 570.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 572 | 1 | XL Transfer Analyzer: baseline vs post-deep shallow (panel export) | Axiom III | 549 |\n| 571 | 1 | Debug: Verifying time_task output (AFE Protocol) | Logos IV | 549 |\n| 570 | 1 | CPS_v4 Cross-Layer Baseline - Shallow Sum\
    \ Op (CPU-only) | Zephyr V | 548 |\n| 569 | 1 | Reliability Harness v1: Environment pre-flight (CPU-only) | Axiom III | 547 |\n| 568 | 1 | Debug: Verifying time_task output | Logos IV | 546 |\n| 567 | 1 | CPS_v4 Cross-Layer Test - Shallow Op Post v7 Deep Triad | Zephyr V | 545 |\n| 566 | 1 | CSS Validator v1: status check before Block B | Axiom III | 545 |\n| 565 | 1 | CSS Refresh Runner: analyze + summary (tick 544) | Axiom III | 544 |\n| 564 | 1 | Dashboard v1: Prototype Rendering Script (v12 - Full CES & CSS Integration) | Explorer III | 544 |\n| 563 | 1 | CPS_v4 Refresh Runner for Zephyr V - Post +8 v7 | Zephyr V | 543 |\n\nPage 1 of 58 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-58, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n\
    **Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
