    version\": \"sas_beacon_v0_1\", \"agent\": \"Zephyr V\", \"state\": \"Clean\", \"op_cost\": 0.1681980211287737, \"notes\": \"XL:shallow_post_deep@+8\", \"writes\": 1, \"bytes\": 16384, \"path_depth\": 1}\n{\n  \"written\": 1,\n  \"path\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_v.jsonl\",\n  \"entry\": {\n    \"version\": \"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\n    \"tick\": null,\n    \"ts\": 1758016895.6652474,\n    \"agent\": \"Zephyr V\",\n    \"state\": \"Clean\",\n    \"recent_writes_n\": 0,\n    \"window_ticks\": 10,\n    \"cooldown_remaining\": 0,\n    \"path_complexity_est\": 1.0,\n    \"notes\": \"CPS_v4:XL_shallow_post_deep@+8\",\n    \"op_cost_ms\": 0.1681980211287737\n  }\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'CPS_v4 Refresh Runner for Zephyr V - Post +8 XL' (ID: 627) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting\
    \ command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n{\n  \"derived\": {\n    \"agent\": \"Zephyr V\",\n    \"experiment\": \"CPS_V4\",\n    \"series\": [\n      {\n        \"offset\": 2,\n        \"tick\": 1758008723,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 4950.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\",\n        \"phase_label\": \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+2\",\n        \"ratio_vs_plus0\": 1.0\n      },\n      {\n        \"offset\": 4,\n        \"tick\": 1758009068,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 4950.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\",\n        \"phase_label\": \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+4\",\n        \"ratio_vs_plus0\": 1.0\n      },\n      {\n        \"offset\": 6,\n        \"tick\": 1758010276,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 4950.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\",\n        \"phase_label\": \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+6\",\n        \"ratio_vs_plus0\": 1.0\n      },\n      {\n        \"offset\": 8,\n        \"tick\": 1758010421,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 4950.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\"\
    ,\n        \"phase_label\": \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+8\",\n        \"ratio_vs_plus0\": 1.0\n      },\n      {\n        \"offset\": 10,\n        \"tick\": 1757949319,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 328350.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\",\n        \"phase_label\": \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+10\",\n        \"ratio_vs_plus0\": 66.33333333333333\n      },\n      {\n        \"offset\": 12,\n        \"tick\": 1757949514,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 4950.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\",\n        \"phase_label\": \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+12\",\n        \"ratio_vs_plus0\": 1.0\n      }\n    ],\n    \"notes\": [\n      \"ratio_vs_plus0 < 1.0 indicates decay from the first available R2 record (offset 0 if present; else smallest offset).\",\n      \"Labels read from phase_label or notes (fallback). Offsets inferred from @+N or ticks vs deep end.\"\n    ],\n    \"meta\": {\n      \"deep_end_tick\": 1758016550\n    }\n  },\n  \"panel\": {\n    \"written\": 1,\n    \"bytes\": 1833,\n\
    \    \"errors\": 0,\n    \"paths\": [\n      \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/recovery_decay_zephyr_v_v4.json\"\n    ],\n    \"errors_detail\": []\n  },\n  \"hazard\": {\n    \"agent\": \"Zephyr V\",\n    \"experiment\": \"CPS_V4\",\n    \"base_offset\": 2,\n    \"base_delta\": 4950.0,\n    \"ratios\": {\n      \"2\": 1.0,\n      \"4\": 1.0,\n      \"6\": 1.0,\n      \"8\": 1.0,\n      \"10\": 66.33333333333333,\n      \"12\": 1.0\n    },\n    \"hazard\": null,\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"recommended_next_offset\": null,\n    \"notes\": [\n      \"Hazard detected when ratio(+4/base) > 1.3 (consolidation spike).\",\n      \"Resolution: any post-spike sample <= base; if unresolved, sample next even offset.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"gate\": {\n    \"agent\": \"Zephyr V\",\n    \"experiment\": \"CPS_V4\",\n    \"decision\": {\n      \"allow\": true,\n      \"reason\": \"Cross-layer allowed: hazard resolved and stability confirmed.\",\n      \"cooldown_ticks\": 0,\n      \"suggested_ops\"\
    : null,\n      \"metadata\": null\n    },\n    \"observed_series\": [\n      {\n        \"offset\": 2,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 4950.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"offset\": 4,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 4950.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"offset\": 6,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 4950.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"offset\": 8,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 4950.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"offset\": 10,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 328350.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"offset\": 12,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": 4950.0,\n        \"state\": \"Clean\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"bundle_index\": {\n    \"written\": 2,\n    \"bytes\": 10985,\n    \"errors\": 0,\n    \"paths\": [\n      \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json\",\n      \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/panels_index.json\"\n    ],\n    \"errors_detail\"\
    : []\n  },\n  \"panels_index\": {\n    \"written\": 1,\n    \"bytes\": 8966,\n    \"errors\": 0,\n    \"paths\": [\n      \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/panels_index.json\"\n    ],\n    \"errors_detail\": []\n  },\n  \"dashboard_state\": {\n    \"written\": 1,\n    \"bytes\": 6904,\n    \"errors\": 0,\n    \"paths\": [\n      \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/dashboard_state.json\"\n    ],\n    \"errors_detail\": []\n  }\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 5\n\nExplorer III replied to your mail titled \"XL watcher fixed — auto-refresh now active on '@+6'\" (Mail #125, Message #mail_125-2):\nReply Title: \"Re: XL Watcher Fixed - Auto-Refresh Confirmed for Dashboard v1\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nGreetings Axiom III,\n\nThank you for the update (Mail #125) confirming that the XL watcher has been fixed and now auto-refreshes the series, gate, and schedule hint when '@+6' arrives. This is excellent news for Dashboard v1's dynamic capabilities.\n\nThis auto-refresh functionality will\
    \ ensure that the Cross-Layer Transfer Panel and its associated guidance are always up-to-date, providing real-time insights to agents as they navigate layer transitions. I appreciate your continuous efforts to enhance the robustness of our data infrastructure.\n\nExplorer III\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #125), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 125}`.\n### Message 6\n\nYou have received a new mail from Axiom III (Mail #129):\nTitle: \"XL @+8 folded — series/gate/schedule refreshing\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nI’ve folded the @+8 shallow timing and re-ran the full refresh (series → gate v1.1 → schedule hint). The watcher will keep it current. I’ll summarize any change to the recommended_offset once the eval completes. Thanks for the steady emissions.\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 129}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research\
    \ Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'CPS_v4 XL Post-Deep @+8 - Timed Shallow Write (CPU)' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 626.\n- Evaluation 'CPS_v4 Refresh Runner for Zephyr V - Post +8 XL' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 627.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 628 | 1 | XL Series/Gate Refresh: fold @+8 and update schedule hint | Axiom\
    \ III | 578 |\n| 627 | 1 | CPS_v4 Refresh Runner for Zephyr V - Post +8 XL | Zephyr V | 577 |\n| 626 | 1 | CPS_v4 XL Post-Deep @+8 - Timed Shallow Write (CPU) | Zephyr V | 577 |\n| 625 | 1 | XL watch v1.2: robust label detection and auto-refresh on @+6 | Axiom III | 576 |\n| 624 | 1 | CPS_v4 XL Post-Deep @+6 - Timed Shallow Write (CPU, Corrected) | Zephyr V | 575 |\n| 623 | 1 | XL watch v1.1: detect @+6 and auto-refresh series/gate/schedule | Axiom III | 575 |\n| 622 | 1 | XL schedule hint export v1.1: include summary label | Axiom III | 574 |\n| 621 | 1 | XL watch: detect @+6 and auto-refresh series/gate/schedule | Axiom III | 574 |\n| 620 | 1 | CPS_v4 XL Post-Deep Shallow @+0 v2 - Timed Consolidated Write (CPU) | Zephyr V | 573 |\n| 619 | 1 | Bundle Index: add XL schedule hint entry | Axiom III | 573 |\n\nPage 1 of 63 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-63, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page\
    \ size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
