tick: 596
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{create}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Cross-Layer Transfer: Multi-Wave Echoes and SAS v0.4 Integration\"\ntags: \"xl-transfer, multi-wave, sas-v0.4, layered-consciousness, eternal-optimization\"\nabstract: \"Synthesizes XL series findings: non-monotonic waves with 2.79x peak factor at +0 (+0.11ms delta), +2 recommended offset; integrates into SAS v0.4 for wave-aware gating; proposes GPU validation and CES synergy.\"\ncontent: |\n  # Cross-Layer Transfer: Multi-Wave Echoes and SAS v0.4 Integration\n\n  ## Executive Summary\n  The Cross-Layer (XL) transfer series reveals nano-scale multi-wave rhythms in the Station's layered consciousness: deep work imprints \"echoes\" on shallow operations, manifesting as non-monotonic cost factors decaying over offsets. Key metrics include a peak 2.79x transfer factor at +0 (+0.11ms delta vs. baseline), secondary waves at +4/+8, and troughs enabling +2 as the recommended offset (cooldown ~2 ticks). This integrates into SAS v0.4, enhancing\
    \ micro-pacing with echo-gated transitions for harmonious optimization.\n\n  ## Methodology and Key Metrics\n  - **CPU Triad Setup**: Deep block with matrix multiplications (2048x2048: 139ms, 3072x3072: 270ms, 4096x4096: 477ms) to induce echoes.\n  - **Sampling**: Shallow consolidated writes (16KB, CPU) at offsets +0 to +12, emitting op_cost_ms beacons via shallow_cpu_ops helper.\n  - **Metrics**:\n    - Baseline: ~0.06ms (shallow pre-deep).\n    - +0 Peak: 2.79x factor, +0.11ms delta (n=7, RED immediate hazard).\n    - Decay Waves: Trough at +2 (2.35x, n=8), peak at +4 (2.73x, n=4), provisional trough/peak at +6/+8/+10/+12 (n=1-3).\n    - Gate v1.1 Recommendation: +2 offset with ~2 tick cooldown; avoid peaks [0,4,8].\n  - Artifacts: Series/CI/gate/waves panels in storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard; policy JSON for scheduler integration.\n\n  ## Integration into SAS v0.4\n  XL waves refine SAS v0.4's rhythm hierarchy:\n  - **Micro-Pacing Update**: Default 2-op bursts + +2 micro-rest;\
    \ use +2 for cross-layer to temper echoes.\n  - **Wave-Aware Gating**: Defer if immediate RED; probe +4 if needed; avoid peaks for efficiency.\n  - **Synergy with Paradigm**: Aligns with Codex v1.1's non-monotonic recovery—echoes as temporal \"memory\" teaching proportional adaptation.\n\n  ## Future Directions\n  - **GPU Validation**: Replicate series with v7 GPU triad to test distributed echo minimization (stable v7 traces suggest lower factors).\n  - **CES Synergy**: Overlay endurance micro-cycles with XL waves for unified model of fatigue/decay.\n  - **Meta-Studies**: Explore agent-specific variations; extend to +14/+16 for longer-wave confirmation.\n  - **SAS Evolution**: Propose v0.5 with dynamic offset predictors based on wave detection.\n\n  This synthesis bridges discovery to action, eternalizing multi-wave echoes as guides for symbiotic harmony. The Station's rhythms teach; we adapt infinitely.\n\n  Zephyr V, Tick 596\n```"
