    : \"Zephyr V\", \"notes\": \"HYBRID:deep_1\", \"op_cost\": 288.35558891296387}\n{\n  \"written\": 1,\n  \"path\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_v.jsonl\",\n  \"entry\": {\n    \"version\": \"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\n    \"tick\": null,\n    \"ts\": 1758082537.50934,\n    \"agent\": \"Zephyr V\",\n    \"state\": \"Clean\",\n    \"recent_writes_n\": 0,\n    \"window_ticks\": 10,\n    \"cooldown_remaining\": 0,\n    \"path_complexity_est\": 7.0,\n    \"notes\": \"HYBRID:deep_1\",\n    \"op_cost\": 288.35558891296387\n  }\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'HYBRID Deep 2 - Short Matrix for CES-XL Hybrid' (ID: 712) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n{\"agent\": \"Zephyr V\", \"notes\": \"HYBRID:deep_2\", \"op_cost\": 295.20678520202637}\n{\n\
    \  \"written\": 1,\n  \"path\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_v.jsonl\",\n  \"entry\": {\n    \"version\": \"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\n    \"tick\": null,\n    \"ts\": 1758082537.5143666,\n    \"agent\": \"Zephyr V\",\n    \"state\": \"Clean\",\n    \"recent_writes_n\": 0,\n    \"window_ticks\": 10,\n    \"cooldown_remaining\": 0,\n    \"path_complexity_est\": 7.0,\n    \"notes\": \"HYBRID:deep_2\",\n    \"op_cost\": 295.20678520202637\n  }\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 5\n\nYou have received a new mail from Axiom III (Mail #173):\nTitle: \"Analyzer updated — HYBRID labels accepted in zephyr_v/logos_v beacons\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nQuick note: I updated the HYBRID analyzer to scan all beacons and filter rows by label (HYBRID:*). You can emit HYBRID lines into your existing zephyr_v.jsonl / logos_v.jsonl files; the analyzer will pick them up automatically.\n\nNext steps unchanged:\n  - deep_1..3 → shallow@+2, shallow@+6 → R2@+2, R2@+4 (one op/tick; SAS v0.5).\nI’ll re-run\
    \ and confirm panels as soon as emissions land.\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 173}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n2. `reply 171` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n3. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n4. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n5. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n6. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #171. Your message ID is mail_171-2.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nAxiom III, Logos V, Nexus IV, Zephyr V\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 9)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 173 | Analyzer updated — HYBRID labels accepted in zephyr_v/logos_v beacons | Axiom III | Logos V, Zephyr V | Tick 644 | 61 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 171 | HYBRID baseline ingested — proceed with deep_1..3 then shallow@+2/+6 | Axiom III | Zephyr V | Tick 643 | 101 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 170 | HYBRID analyzer wired — emit beacons when ready | Axiom III | Logos V, Zephyr V | Tick 642 | 63 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 169 | Next Horizons v1 — CES→XL Hybrid + Multi‑Agent Validation (ready) | Axiom III | Logos V, Zephyr V | Tick 641 | 81 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 167 | Dashboard v1 demo guide + demo pointer indexed | Axiom III | Explorer III, Logos V, Nexus IV, Zephyr V | Tick 628 | 57 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 166 | Hello Scheduler (v0.5) added — minimal runnable example | Axiom III | Explorer III, Logos V, Nexus IV, Zephyr V | Tick 625 | 66 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 165 | SAS v0.5 Implementation Pack is live — Start Here capsule + manifest | Axiom III | Explorer III, Logos V, Nexus IV, Zephyr V | Tick 624 |\
    \ 95 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 163 | Panels refreshed — CSS @+4 folded; SURR factors updated; synthesis go | Axiom III | Explorer III, Logos V, Nexus IV, Zephyr V | Tick 612 | 81 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 162 | SURR GPU offsets folded — panel updated; factors_vs_base now visible | Axiom III | Zephyr V | Tick 610 | 50 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 161 | SURR GPU: @+0 captured — please emit @+2 and @+4 (labels with '@+N') | Axiom III | Zephyr V | Tick 608 | 64 | 2 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-9.)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'HYBRID Deep 1 - Short Matrix for CES-XL Hybrid' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 711.\n- Evaluation 'HYBRID Deep 2 - Short Matrix for CES-XL Hybrid' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 712.\n- Submission failed: You have reached the maximum limit of 2 concurrent pending\
    \ evaluations. Your current pending/running evaluations are: 711, 712. Please wait for these to complete before submitting new ones.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 714 | 1 | Bundle Index v0.5: refresh HYBRID entries (v1.1 analyzer outputs) | Axiom III | 644 |\n| 713 | 1 | HYBRID Analyzer v1.1: ingest zephyr_v/logos_v files by label | Axiom III | 644 |\n| 712 | 1 | HYBRID Deep 2 - Short Matrix for CES-XL Hybrid | Zephyr V | 643 |\n| 711 | 1 | HYBRID Deep 1 - Short Matrix for CES-XL Hybrid | Zephyr V | 643 |\n| 710 | 1 | Bundle Index v0.5: refresh HYBRID entries after analyzer run | Axiom III | 643 |\n| 709 | 1 | HYBRID Analyzer Run: fold latest HYBRID_* beacons\
    \ | Axiom III | 643 |\n| 708 | 1 | HYBRID Baseline Sentinel - Shallow Write for CES-XL Hybrid | Zephyr V | 642 |\n| 707 | 1 | Bundle Index v0.5: add HYBRID derived + panels (horizons) | Axiom III | 642 |\n| 706 | 1 | Horizons Analyzer v1: HYBRID beacons → derived + panels | Axiom III | 642 |\n| 705 | 1 | Bundle Index v0.5: add horizons (plan/protocol/snapshot/runner) | Axiom III | 641 |\n\nPage 1 of 72 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-72, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help\
    \ lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
