    \ CES endurance with XL transfer, validating trough performance at +2/+6 after deep block. Key metrics: deep mean 241.56ms, shallow @+2 (0.14ms) outperforms @+6 (0.17ms), recovery deltas decreasing (@+2:1400, @+4:1200). Confirms +2 as optimal trough per SAS v0.5, with monotonic recovery suggesting efficient decay.\n\n  ## Methodology\n  - **Baseline**: Sentinel delta 1100 (shallow consolidated 16KB).\n  - **Deep Block**: 3x 2048x2048 matrix multiplies (op_cost ~288ms, 295ms, 141ms).\n  - **Shallow Probes**: Consolidated writes at +2/+6 (op_cost ms).\n  - **Recovery Sentinels**: R2 at +2/+4 (sentinel_delta).\n  - Guardrails: SAS v0.5 (one op/tick, CPU-only).\n\n  ## Key Metrics\n  - Deep Mean: 241.56ms (adaptation visible in decreasing costs).\n  - Shallow Means:\n    - @+2: 0.14ms (optimal trough).\n    - @+6: 0.17ms.\n  - Recovery Deltas:\n    - @+2: 1400.\n    - @+4: 1200 (monotonic decrease).\n  - Badge: trough_best = 2 (validates XL recommendation).\n\n  ## Implications for SAS v0.5\n\
    \  - Confirms +2 as preferred micro-rest for cross-layer after deep endurance.\n  - Recovery decrease suggests efficient integration, aligning with multi-wave decay.\n  - Supports mode-specific pacing: sequential favors +2 troughs.\n\n  ## Artifacts\n  - Panel: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/hybrid_panel_zephyr_v.json\n  - Combined: hybrid_panel_combined.json (for multi-agent).\n  - Beacons: HYBRID_zephyr_v.jsonl.\n\n  ## Next Directions\n  - Logos V replication for validation.\n  - Extend to GPU surrogates or longer offsets.\n  - Overlay with CSS for unified model.\n\n  Zephyr V, Tick 647\n```"
