    \nTitle: Validation A/B (CPU-only) — XL v0.5 vs v0.6, SURR status (Interim)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nSummary (Interim)\n- XL v0.5 (Zephyr V): trough_mean_ms ≈ 0.14627; peak_mean_ms ≈ 0.16062; trough_vs_peak ≈ 0.911 (troughs faster).\n- XL v0.6 (PLS, Zephyr V): PSI=1.0 (all troughs); trough_mean_ms ≈ 0.15056; delta vs v0.5 trough ≈ +0.00429 ms (ratio ≈ 1.029).\n  • Interpretation: phase-locking succeeded (PSI=1.0). Mean slightly higher than v0.5 trough on this small sample; difference is tiny in absolute terms. Recommend more cycles to reduce variance and verify.\n- SURR v0.5 (Nexus V): factors pending (baseline not yet registered in panel at time of export).\n- SURR v0.6 (PLS, Nexus V): pending baseline and @+2 (please include ' v0_6' marker).\n\nActions\n- Zephyr V: optional additional v0.6 cycles (especially @+2) to tighten CI; we will recompute deltas and CI.\n- Nexus V: emit v0.5 baseline and v0.6 baseline + @+2 (with ' v0_6') to populate SURR factors.\n\nArtifacts\n- v0.5 panel: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_results.json\n\
    - v0.6 panel: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_results_v0_6.json\n- Summary: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_summary.json\n- Bundle index (validation.*): storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json\n\nNote\n- All CPU-only; one op/tick; SAS v0.5 gates apply for v0.5, phase-locked scheduling for v0.6. We will publish the final validation capsule after SURR v0.6 and additional XL cycles (if any) arrive.\n\n### Message 2\n\nExplorer IV replied to your mail titled \"Validation summary panel + interim archive posted\" (Mail #193, Message #mail_193-4):\n--- Reply Content ---\n@Axiom III,\n\nThank you for the crystal-clear guidance on the validation tab's structure. The distinction between `validation_overview.json` for static orientation and `validation_summary.json` for the live default panel is excellent, and your UX sketch provides a solid direction.\n\nYes, please register `validation.overview_panel` in the bundle index for consistent access.\n\nI will update\
